{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:49:52.059Z","ordinal":23788,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_04290251e26d63f4016accd76d42ec8191a5abff6703da2917","status":"completed","call_id":"call_3b3bce82c47542efa3eae9899132d96d","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /tmp/tally-final-onboarding-20261012/docs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md\\n@@\\n-- **cfo.ai Ari task context:** a separate default-no prompt can publish one operational report per attempt to organization-scoped cfo.ai memory. This is shared with members of the selected workspace. Reports include task title/ID and issue link, repository, model/tier and configured rates, token usage when reported, estimated cost and its provenance, attempt ceiling/outcome/routing decision, budget snapshot, and PR/Entire/Neatlogs/cfo.ai links. Reports exclude issue bodies, source code and diffs, worker prompts and transcripts, raw trace contents, and credentials. Dry runs do not publish reports. The local ledger remains Tally's record; a failed memory write does not fail verified work and is reported in the run result.\\n+- **cfo.ai Ari task context:** a separate default-no prompt can add or update one Tally-managed interpretation note on the selected scenario page and publish one operational report per attempt to organization-scoped cfo.ai memory. The note is changed only when it carries Tally's marker; other page blocks are left alone. Memory reports are shared with members of the selected workspace. They include task title/ID and issue link, repository, model/tier and configured rates, token usage when reported, estimated cost and its provenance, attempt ceiling/outcome/routing decision, budget snapshot, and PR/Entire/Neatlogs/cfo.ai links. Reports exclude issue bodies, source code and diffs, worker prompts and transcripts, raw trace contents, and credentials. Dry runs do not publish reports. The local ledger remains Tally's record; a failed memory write does not fail verified work and is reported in the run result.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1300b-17e6-7e20-bf7a-c9594d868dc3","create_time":1791809389.263353}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-12T12:49:52.122Z","ordinal":23789,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a129b0-6007-7bd2-a48b-906c7b0f50e6","turn_id":"01a1300b-17e6-7e20-bf7a-c9594d868dc3","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-15a73d86-f9b4-4742-9aad-8fec4b865074","changes":{"/tmp/tally-final-onboarding-20261012/docs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -22,3 +22,3 @@\n - **cfo.ai table creation:** if required tables are missing, Tally displays their names, rows, formulas, and starting values, then asks before creating them. Existing tables and model data are not reset. Table creation is an external cfo.ai write.\n-- **cfo.ai Ari task context:** a separate default-no prompt can publish one operational report per attempt to organization-scoped cfo.ai memory. This is shared with members of the selected workspace. Reports include task title/ID and issue link, repository, model/tier and configured rates, token usage when reported, estimated cost and its provenance, attempt ceiling/outcome/routing decision, budget snapshot, and PR/Entire/Neatlogs/cfo.ai links. Reports exclude issue bodies, source code and diffs, worker prompts and transcripts, raw trace contents, and credentials. Dry runs do not publish reports. The local ledger remains Tally's record; a failed memory write does not fail verified work and is reported in the run result.\n+- **cfo.ai Ari task context:** a separate default-no prompt can add or update one Tally-managed interpretation note on the selected scenario page and publish one operational report per attempt to organization-scoped cfo.ai memory. The note is changed only when it carries Tally's marker; other page blocks are left alone. Memory reports are shared with members of the selected workspace. They include task title/ID and issue link, repository, model/tier and configured rates, token usage when reported, estimated cost and its provenance, attempt ceiling/outcome/routing decision, budget snapshot, and PR/Entire/Neatlogs/cfo.ai links. Reports exclude issue bodies, source code and diffs, worker prompts and transcripts, raw trace contents, and credentials. Dry runs do not publish reports. The local ledger remains Tally's record; a failed memory write does not fail verified work and is reported in the run result.\n - **Neatlogs and cfo.ai software setup:** Tally bundles the Neatlogs SDK and connects to cfo.ai through its built-in MCP OAuth flow. Neither requires a separate CLI/package installation. Creating keys, authorizing cfo.ai, connecting history, and installing machine-wide Neatlogs hooks remain separate choices.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /tmp/tally-final-onboarding-20261012/docs/HUMAN_APPROVALS.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1791809392122,"completed_at_ms":1791809392122}}
